.TH DW 1 "August 2026" "vst-ace" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dw \- the DW\-8000 engine and the native plug\-in hosts, in one program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dw
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dw
is the entry point to
.BR vst-ace ,
which loads and runs audio plug\-ins built for Windows, macOS and Linux as
native code on Linux \(em not under Wine and not emulated.
.PP
With no command it opens a window:
.B pestudio
if this machine has Qt6,
.B dwstudio
if it has GTK4, and the one matching the desktop if it has both.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B \-\-qt ", " \-\-gtk
Force one window or the other. So does setting
.B DW_GUI
to \fBqt\fR or \fBgtk\fR.
.TP
.B pe " [\fIdir\fR|\fIbank.json\fR]"
The Qt6 window: load and play real plug\-ins natively \(em Windows VST2 and
VST3, native Linux VST3, and each plug\-in's own editor.
.TP
.B gui
The GTK4 window: instruments, patches, drums and a Juno panel.
.TP
.B peload " \fIplug\-in\fR [\fIoptions\fR]"
The same hosts from the command line.
.B \-\-params
lists every exposed parameter,
.B \-\-render \fIout.wav\fR
renders,
.B \-\-detect
reports what the file is, and
.B \-\-patch
/
.B \-\-pick
apply a patch. Run
.B dw peload \-\-help
for the rest.
.TP
.B live
Play live, from a MIDI controller or the computer keyboard.
.TP
.B play " \fIpreset\fR"
Play one preset of the reimplemented DW\-8000 engine, by index or by part of
its name. No plug\-in is loaded.
.TP
.B demo
A short tour of the factory presets.
.TP
.B list
List the current bank's programs.
.TP
.B render " \fIdir\fR"
Render the whole bank to \fIdir\fR.
.TP
.B keys
The note map, and what this terminal does with a held key.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VST_ROOT
The plug\-in corpus: a directory holding
.IR windows/ ,
.I linux/
and
.I macos/
subdirectories. An installed copy looks for
.I ~/vst
when this is unset. It is what lets a bare plug\-in name be used in place of a
path; anything given as a path is unaffected.
.TP
.B FB7999
Path to a copy of the FB\-7999 plug\-in binary. The wavetable and all three
preset banks are read straight out of it, so nothing has to be extracted
first, and the engine commands need it.
.TP
.B BANK
\fBA\fR (the default), \fBB\fR or \fB6000\fR.
.TP
.BR NOTE ", " GATE ", " LEN
What gets rendered, and for how long.
.TP
.BR PELOAD32 ", " PESERVE
Override the paths to the helper programs. Both are found beside the host
otherwise, in
.IR /usr/lib/vst\-ace .
.TP
.B PELOAD_DLL_PATH
Colon\-separated directories to search for a Windows runtime DLL a plug\-in
needs at load time.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/vst\-ace/
The hosts:
.BR peload ", " peserve ", " pestudio " and " dwstudio .
.TP
.I /usr/share/vst\-ace/patches/
Patch banks, as JSON. Hand one to
.B dw pe
to open the plug\-ins it names with their patches loaded.
.SH NOTES
Plug\-in editors embed through an X11 window id, so both windows ask for the
X11 backend under Wayland; XWayland is enough. Override
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORM
or
.B GDK_BACKEND
for a native Wayland window and no native editors.
.PP
Plug\-ins are hosted out of process by default: a browser loads a hundred of
them in a session, and one that faults should not end it.
.PP
This package hosts 64\-bit plug\-ins.
.B dw peload32
needs a 32\-bit toolchain that Debian and Ubuntu do not carry the libraries
for, so it is not built here; build from source for 32\-bit Windows plug\-ins.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project documentation in
.IR /usr/share/doc/vst\-ace/ ,
and
.UR https://github.com/spacestate1/VST-ace
.UE .
